From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: emuTOS-MCD <darekadumon@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 05:35:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 130/190] segacd2: the timeshare was reading the wrong half of
 the status word

CDCSTAT does no work. It is five instructions comparing the sector
ring's head and tail (US 0x1D10) and never touches hardware, so polling
it drives nothing -- the ring is filled by the firmware's interrupts.
That settles the shape: a swap-in/call/swap-out cannot work, and the
firmware has to be resident with its vectors live for a whole read.
Which is what _segacd_bios_read already does.

And then it waited for the drive like this:

    move.w (a0),d0
    andi.w #0x00FF,d0        <- the low byte
    cmpi.w #0x0004,d0
    cmpi.w #0x0001,d0

The drive state is in the high byte. Doom CD32X Fusion's sub program
(ROM 0xC7E) reads `move.w (a0),d0 / lsr.w #8,d0 / cmpi.b #$40 /
cmpi.b #$10`, and our own wake, written from it this afternoon, gets
state 2 out of hardware doing the same. This masked the half the state
does not live in, so it never matched, brd_wait_init spun to its
200-frame timeout on every visit, and the read went ahead against a
drive nothing had confirmed.

That is exactly the failure this timeshare has reported since it was
written: "no sector was ever announced", with the drive at state 0.

Fixed to the nibble rather than the whole byte, because hardware
reports 0x2n and a byte compare against 0x20 would miss it, and 2 is
accepted alongside 4 and 1 -- this project's own note says a CD boot
reads 1, 2 or 4.

DRV_INIT goes back on by default with it. It was switched off on the
grounds that "no Sega code that reads a sector calls DRV_INIT to do
it"; Doom's sub program calls it every frame its CDBSTAT comes back
wrong, along with FDRSET and CDCSTOP, and refuses every command until
the drive answers. That is a shipping Mode 1 CD reader contradicting
the grounds directly. It also never mattered which way the flag was
set, because the wait behind it could not succeed either way.
---
 bios/segacd2.S | 43 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++------
 1 file changed, 37 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/bios/segacd2.S b/bios/segacd2.S
index 73caf8c..fb077b0 100644
--- a/bios/segacd2.S
+++ b/bios/segacd2.S
@@ -247,7 +247,19 @@ _segacd_bios_ctrl:                      // $FF8037 and $FF8033 on entry
 _segacd_bios_lost:                      // mask bits seen switched off
         .word   0                       //    at any point during a visit
 _segacd_bios_drvinit:                   // whether to wake with DRV_INIT
-        .byte   0
+        // On, and that reverses a correction.
+        //
+        // It was turned off on the grounds that "no Sega code that
+        // reads a sector calls DRV_INIT to do it". Doom CD32X Fusion's
+        // sub program does, every frame its CDBSTAT comes back wrong,
+        // together with FDRSET and CDCSTOP, and it will not accept a
+        // command until the drive answers 4 or 1. That is a shipping
+        // Mode 1 CD reader and it contradicts the grounds directly.
+        //
+        // It also stopped mattering what the setting was, because the
+        // wait behind it tested the wrong half of the status word and
+        // could never succeed either way.
+        .byte   1
         .even
 _segacd_bios_st:                        // CDD status, first four nibbles
         .long   0                       //    pairs, as the visit ended
@@ -540,12 +552,31 @@ brd_wait_init:
         move.w  #0x0081,d0              // CDB_STAT
         move.w  d0,50(a5)
         jsr     0x5F22
-        move.w  (a0),d0                 // status: low byte is drive state
-        andi.w  #0x00FF,d0
-        move.w  d0,34(a5)
-        cmpi.w  #0x0004,d0              // paused, ready to be read from
+        // The drive state is in the HIGH byte, not the low one.
+        //
+        // This masked 0x00FF and compared against 4 and 1, so it was
+        // testing a half of the status word the state does not live in.
+        // It therefore never matched, brd_wait_init spun to its
+        // 200-frame timeout on every visit, and the read went ahead
+        // against a drive nothing had confirmed -- which is precisely
+        // the failure this timeshare has always reported: "no sector
+        // was ever announced", with the drive at state 0.
+        //
+        // Doom CD32X Fusion's sub program (ROM 0xC7E) is the reference:
+        // `move.w (a0),d0 / lsr.w #8,d0 / cmpi.b #$40 / cmpi.b #$10`.
+        // The nibble is compared rather than the whole byte because the
+        // low nibble carries other things -- our own wake reported
+        // state 2 on hardware as 0x2n, and a whole-byte compare against
+        // 0x20 would have missed it.
+        move.w  (a0),d0
+        move.w  d0,34(a5)               // the whole word, for the report
+        lsr.w   #8,d0
+        andi.w  #0x00F0,d0              // the drive's own state nibble
+        cmpi.w  #0x0040,d0              // paused, ready to be read from
+        beq     brd_init_done
+        cmpi.w  #0x0020,d0              // and 2, which a CD boot shows
         beq     brd_init_done
-        cmpi.w  #0x0001,d0              // playing, also fine
+        cmpi.w  #0x0010,d0              // playing, also fine
         bne     brd_wait_init
 brd_init_done:
         move.b  #1,_bios_woken
